program	conformance/K91_spawn_brace_captures_nothing_implicitly.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	a spawned brace captures nothing implicitly, and this body names `count`, `label`
meets_expect	yes
log	"error: a spawned brace captures nothing implicitly, and this body names `count`, `label`"
log	"  --> examples/conformance/K91_spawn_brace_captures_nothing_implicitly.saw:28:32"
log	"     |"
log	" 28 |     var spawned = Thread.spawn { count + label.len() }"
log	"     |                                ^"
log	"   hint: name what crosses in the capture list — `Thread.spawn { [count, label] in ... }`. The list IS the body's parameter list: each entry transfers at the spawn, by value, at its own copy tier, and `[move x]` is how a move-only value goes. Everything that crosses a concurrency boundary is spelled at the crossing"
log	""
log	"1 error(s) generated"
